+# CAM-30 (27.11): #30, "two places where the camera goes into a wall" — the play camera against walls, game-wide
+
+Worktree branch `cam30` of `ccr-c1c2c4b9-dep6ed` from `ffe34e88`. Every result here is **automated runtime only
+(SwiftShader, headless Chromium)**: nobody played it, no real GPU, no frame times on real hardware. Every suite ran with
+`SERVE=1`. Pictures: `captures/cam-30/sheet.png` (before | after, the same walk replayed by input to the same frame).
+
+## What #30 was and how it was looked for
+
+The two places were never written down, so `tests/camwalls.mjs` (new) looks for every place of that kind. At the defaults
+(Follow camera, Far — P100 —, Classic controls) it walks every outdoor area — Citadel, Zeelich, Desert Island with Kesh,
+the Hamalayi, the nine isles, Ballastra's harbour and its two districts — by input (`tests/lib/player.js` P.go, held
+keys) at 60 fps, recording every camera update (`tests/lib/camwalk.js`, `tests/lib/camscan.js`):
+
+- **legs**: each resident's round, stop to stop (the residents' routes are the area's paths; an area with fewer than six
+  legs also gets its arrival-to-door paths);
+- **doors**: every door any chapter offers into the area (the chapters' `doors()` by their flags, as door-sweep.mjs sets
+  them, and an outdoor room's own exits): out of its room by input, recorded from the first frame outside, a walk away, a
+  whole turn on the spot with his back to the house, a stand;
+- **buildings**: round every building (the area's scenery volumes at least 2.5 m over the floor at their foot, pieces
+  that touch as one): its corners 1.0 m off the walls, a whole turn at the first corner, then round by input.
+
+The seeds are the game's own data, frozen in `tests/fixtures/cam30-seeds.json`, so the walks are the same before and
+after a fix. 397 walks outdoors (about 400,000 recorded frames), 21 skipped (a start inside something, a door whose room
+has no exit back to it in the state walked, the terminal's ticket dialogue).
+
+Judged per frame, against the drawn opaque triangles round the walk (instanced meshes by instance; foliage cards, glass,
+decals and skinned bodies left out):
+
+- the lens inside anything solid the camera knows (a collider, a scenery volume, the ground);
+- the lens behind a drawn face of a **wall-like** solid (inside it);
+- the **near plane** — its middle and four corners at `cam.near` in front of the lens — inside or within 0.15 m of a
+  wall-like solid (its inside shows, or is about to);
+- a wall-like solid covering him (the lines to his head and his chest both cut, past the near plane) longer than 0.75 s.
+
+Wall-like: the solid round the spot, measured by rays along x, y and z to its faces, has two extents of 1.5 m or more (a
+wall, a roof, a rock face, the ground); an eave's rim, a post, a rail or a branch has one; a lone sheet with no face
+round it in any direction (a gull, a card) is no solid. Listed, not judged: the same with smaller solids, and the lens
+within 0.15 m of a solid but outside it (nothing it draws is cut: the near plane's own test says when it is).
+
+Interiors (the fixed iso camera): every interior room, at each exit (0.25 m and 0.9 m inside it) and each landing, his
+head and chest against the room's own meshes (room-cutaway.mjs's rays; the lids settled as the room camera shows them,
+wire mesh and leaf cards seen through).
+
+RESULTS_PLACEHOLDER
